"comparison": "Both disclosures address the definition and calculation of maximum exposure to loss for VIEs. Citigroup defines maximum loss as assuming default with no recovery from VIE assets. Goldman Sachs defines maximum exposure to loss as the carrying value for interests or notional amount for commitments, explicitly noting it excludes offsetting instruments and does not represent anticipated losses. Both serve to quantify potential downside exposure despite different methodological nuances (Citi's hypothetical 'no recovery' vs. GS's carrying value/notional based on specific interest types).",
