"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both disclosures clarify the limitation of the reporting entity's exposure to loss within VIEs. Citigroup notes that maximum loss assumes the VIE defaults with no recovery from assets held by the VIE. Morgan Stanley states that its exposure to loss in consolidated VIEs is generally limited to the VIE net assets recognized in the financial statements, net of amounts absorbed by third-party variable interest holders. Both highlight that the reported exposure is constrained by the specific structure or recovery expectations, rather than unlimited liability.",
